---
import DocumentTitleBlock from '../../components/DocumentTitleBlock.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../lib/site-config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`How a Capture is checked — ${siteConfig.eventTitle}`}
  description="Why a Garden Crawl Submission can be checked without taking this website’s word for it."
>
  <main id="main" data-document>
    <DocumentTitleBlock>
      <Fragment slot="title">How a Capture is checked</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="lead">
        <p>
          When you make a Capture with Proofmode, the resulting Submission can be checked without taking this
          website&rsquo;s word for it. This page explains that path. Configure the app on the{' '}
          <a href="/proofmode/">Proofmode</a> page. Event rules live on <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Garden Crawl is a public contest that uses this model: original Captures in official Gardens, published so
          others can check them.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
    </DocumentTitleBlock>

    <div class="doc-body">
      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="the-path">
        <h2 id="the-path">The path</h2>
        <p>
          Home teases this chain as glass-to-glass verification. This page is the long form. A Capture moves through
          four stages: Capture, Upload, Attest, and Verify.
        </p>
        <ol class="path-strip">
          <li><span class="mono">01</span> Capture</li>
          <li><span class="mono">02</span> Upload</li>
          <li><span class="mono">03</span> Attest</li>
          <li><span class="mono">04</span> Verify</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="capture">
        <h2 id="capture">Capture</h2>
        <p>
          At shutter-press, Proofmode creates a Capture and a Proofset &mdash; the cryptographic evidence bundled with
          that Capture. Signing happens on the device. This website does not hold your signing key and does not create
          the Proofset.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Wallet address is the persistent, pseudonymous public identifier associated with your later Attestations.
          It is not your name, email, or phone number. See <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> for what the Public
          submission map does and does not display.
        </p>
        <p>
          This event&rsquo;s unit of competition is an original Capture made with Proofmode&rsquo;s in-app camera, not a
          photo imported from elsewhere or a file stored only on our servers. Setup is on the{' '}
          <a href="/proofmode/">Proofmode</a> page. Validity rules are on <a href="/compete/">Compete</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="upload">
        <h2 id="upload">Upload</h2>
        <p>
          If the only copy of a Capture lives as a filename on one organization&rsquo;s servers, anyone checking it has
          to trust that organization still has the file, has not changed it, and will keep serving it.
        </p>
        <p>
          IPFS addresses Capture media and related Proofset files by a content identifier (CID). The CID is derived
          from a hash of the bytes. Change a byte, and the identifier changes. An Attestation can point at those files
          so reviewers and the Public submission map retrieve the same bytes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Organizer pinning, unpinning, and takedown are explained on{' '}
          <a href="/privacy/#decentralized-storage">Privacy&rsquo;s decentralized storage</a> and{' '}
          <a href="/privacy/#removal">removal</a> sections. This page does not restate those rules.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="attest">
        <h2 id="attest">Attest</h2>
        <p>
          The chain is a shared public ledger. Proofmode publishes the Attestation there so the claim is not held only
          inside the app or on this campaign site.
        </p>
        <p>
          An Attestation is a structured on-chain claim: this Capture, this Wallet address, this place and time,
          pointing at the CID and Proofset. Anyone can look that Attestation up without asking this website. This site
          does not submit chain activity.
        </p>
        <p>
          Eligibility and prizes rest on that public claim remaining look-uppable, not on a private database on this
          site. An on-chain Attestation is not removed by unpinning media or hiding a Submission on the Public
          submission map. See <a href="/privacy/#decentralized-storage">Privacy&rsquo;s decentralized storage</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="verify">
        <h2 id="verify">Verify</h2>
        <p>
          Checking means reading the ledger, fetching the bytes by CID, and confirming they still match &mdash; without
          this website as intermediary for that check. A checker confirms the file hashes match the anchored CID, the
          C2PA manifest is valid, and the ledger receipt matches.
        </p>
        <p>
          A checkable Attestation is a signed claim of place and time. It is not proof that the GPS signal was
          authentic.
        </p>
        <p>
          This website is not the verifier of record. Judges, other participants, or a stranger can check.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="checker">
        <h2 id="checker">What a checker looks at</h2>
        <dl class="details">
          <dt>Wallet address</dt>
          <dd>The persistent, pseudonymous public identifier associated with the Attestations.</dd>
          <dt>CID</dt>
          <dd>How the Capture media and related Proofset bytes are addressed on IPFS.</dd>
          <dt>Attestation</dt>
          <dd>The public ledger claim a checker looks up.</dd>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="location-protocol">
        <h2 id="location-protocol">Location Protocol</h2>
        <p>
          Location Protocol is a specification for portable, signed location records. It is not a camera app and not
          this website.
        </p>
        <p>
          Proofmode uses it so the place-and-time claim is bound to the Capture media by CID and can be checked outside
          this site. The in-app control is Location Protocol Attestation; how to turn it on is on the{' '}
          <a href="/proofmode/">Proofmode</a> page.
        </p>
        <figure class="envelope">
          <figcaption class="visually-hidden">
            Location Protocol wraps place, time, and CID. Proofmode publishes that as the event Attestation.
          </figcaption>
          <div class="envelope-box" aria-hidden="true">
            <p class="mono envelope-kicker">Location Protocol</p>
            <ul class="envelope-fields">
              <li>Place</li>
              <li>Time</li>
              <li>CID</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="envelope-foot">Published as the event Attestation</p>
          </div>
        </figure>
        <p>
          This Garden Crawl is that standard used in a public contest: official Gardens, original Captures, Submissions
          others can check.
        </p>
        <p>
          Location Protocol was designed by EASIER Data in collaboration with Astral. Proofmode, from the Guardian
          Project, is the Capture app that emits the Attestation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="event-rules">
        <h2 id="event-rules">Event rules</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> is the canonical event-rules page. Read it before you install Proofmode or
          make a Capture. Use these sections rather than this teaching page for the lists and warnings:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/privacy/#not-public">What is not public</a></li>
          <li><a href="/privacy/#may-be-public">What may be public</a></li>
          <li><a href="/privacy/#coordinates">Precise Capture coordinates</a></li>
          <li><a href="/privacy/#sensitive-content">Identifiable people and sensitive content</a></li>
          <li><a href="/privacy/#decentralized-storage">Decentralized storage</a></li>
          <li><a href="/privacy/#removal">Requesting media removal</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="further-reading">
        <h2 id="further-reading">Further reading</h2>
        <p>Optional background. The wording on this page is the published explanation for the event.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <ExternalLink href="https://spec.decentralizedgeo.org/">Location Protocol specification</ExternalLink>
          </li>
          <li>
            <ExternalLink href="https://easierdata.org/updates/2025/2025-05-19-location-protocol-spec">
              EASIER Data: Location Protocol specification
            </ExternalLink>
          </li>
          <li>
            <ExternalLink href="https://easierdata.org/updates/2025/2025-11-17-preserving-proof-proofmode-integration">
              How Proofmode stores proofs and location claims
            </ExternalLink>
          </li>
          <li>
            <ExternalLink
              href="https://gitlab.com/guardianproject/proofmode/proofmode-android/-/blob/main/docs/location-protocol/tutorial-create-location-attestations.md"
            >
              Proofmode: Create location attestations
            </ExternalLink>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  main#main[data-document] {
    max-width: 1760px;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .doc-body {
    padding: 48px 48px 84px;
  }

  .doc-section {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg, 2rem);
  }

  .doc-section:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  h2 {
    max-width: 74ch;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm, 1rem);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  p,
  ul,
  ol,
  dl,
  figure {
    max-width: 74ch;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-2);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm, 1rem);
  }

  p:last-child,
  ul:last-child,
  ol:last-child,
  dl:last-child,
  figure:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  ul,
  ol.path-strip {
    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
  }

  .path-strip {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.55rem 0;
    list-style: none;
    padding-inline-start: 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .path-strip li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .path-strip li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '→';
    margin-inline: 0.65rem 0.15rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }

  .path-strip .mono {
    color: var(--text-3);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .details {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-xs, 0.75rem) var(--space-sm, 1rem);
  }

  .details dt {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .details dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .envelope {
    margin: var(--space-sm, 1rem) 0;
  }

  .envelope-box {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .envelope-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }

  .envelope-fields {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .envelope-fields li {
    border: 1px solid var(--border-2);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .envelope-foot {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-3);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .doc-body {
      padding: 32px 18px 56px;
    }

    .path-strip {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.35rem;
    }

    .path-strip li:not(:last-child)::after {
      content: none;
    }

    .details {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.2rem 0;
    }

    .details dt {
      margin-top: 0.65rem;
    }

    .details dt:first-child {
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
